  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Alemtuzumab is a monoclonal antibody used to treat multiple sclerosis and certain leukemias, including chronic lymphocytic leukemia and T-cell prolymphocytic leukemia. It remains authorised in the European Union, though one EU product has been withdrawn, and it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420164&quot;>Wikidata Q420164</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>alemtuzumab</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01XC04, L04AA34, L04AG06</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00087&quot;>DB00087</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420164&quot;>Q420164</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>145454 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end Alemtuzumab;
